            <ArticleTitle>Coronary artery vasospasm and acute myocarditis: a rare association.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1879-88</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Coronary vasospasm is one cause of chest pain in patients with acute myocarditis. This is a rare association, with few cases reported in the literature. The authors describe a case of acute myocarditis in which presentation mimicked acute myocardial infarction. During hospitalization severe angina recurred twice, accompanied by transient ST-segment elevation in different locations. The hypothesis of coronary vasospasm is discussed. The role of cardiac magnetic resonance imaging in this context is highlighted.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
